//! Replays `fixtures/reference/exec.json.gz`, generated by `tools/refgen/run.sh`: the real
//! upstream execution code (PathingBehavior, PathExecutor, the movements' updateState,
//! LookBehavior, InventoryBehavior, InputOverrideHandler and its break and place helpers,
//! PathingControlManager, the processes) run tick by tick around a simulated client
//! (`ExecRefGen.java`), which `common::sim` mirrors around the port.
//!
//! Every tick of every scenario is compared: the player's position, motion and rotation (bit
//! for bit), crouching, sprinting, the selected slot, the inputs Baritone forces, whether it
//! drives the movement input, the game mode calls (breaking, placing, inventory swaps, arm
//! swings), the path events, the current path's position and length, the pathing command
//! (type and goal) and the process in control. `REPLAY_TRACE=<scenario name>` prints every
//! tick of that scenario, both sides.
//!
//! The fixture also holds samples of the geometry execution relies on: raytraces
//! (`RayTraceUtils.rayTraceTowards`, i.e. `Level.clip` with outline shapes), block centers
//! (`VecUtils.calculateBlockCenter`), and `RotationUtils.reachable` with the look behavior's
//! aim processor, `playerFeet` and `pathStart`, in a world of assorted shapes.

mod common;

